{
 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Download and convert the raw direct-detection data to JSON\n",
    "\n",
    "This notebook is intended for Google Colab. It discovers the files in `recent_data/raw` on GitHub, downloads supported data files with `wget`, and extracts numeric x-y pairs from CSV, whitespace-delimited TXT, and Excel workbooks. Markdown/README files are not treated as data.\n",
    "\n",
    "Each file is represented as a list of sections. Each section contains a `pairs` list of `[x, y]` values, so a curve looks like `[[\"1.0\", \"2e-45\"], [\"3.0\", \"4e-45\"]]`. Numeric values are JSON strings intentionally: this preserves the original scientific-notation spelling and decimal digits exactly for text files. Excel numeric cells are already stored as spreadsheet numbers, so their original textual spelling cannot always be recovered.\n",
    "\n",
    "For files with multiple table sections (for example, LZ expected-limit bands), each section is kept separate with its header as a label rather than mixing different curves together. The parser selects the last two numeric columns in each data row, which also handles files with a leading row index."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "from pathlib import Path\n",
    "from decimal import Decimal, InvalidOperation\n",
    "import csv\n",
    "import json\n",
    "import re\n",
    "import subprocess\n",
    "import requests\n",
    "\n",
    "# openpyxl is generally installed in Colab, but install it if necessary.\n",
    "try:\n",
    "    import openpyxl\n",
    "except ImportError:\n",
    "    %pip -q install openpyxl\n",
    "    import openpyxl\n",
    "\n",
    "OWNER = \"BrownParticleAstro\"\n",
    "REPO = \"dmtools_notebooks\"\n",
    "REF = \"main\"\n",
    "RAW_DIR = \"recent_data/raw\"\n",
    "WORKDIR = Path(\"/content/dmtools_raw_downloads\")\n",
    "WORKDIR.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Supported data formats. README/Markdown and other non-tabular files are skipped.\n",
    "SUPPORTED = {\".csv\", \".txt\", \".xlsx\", \".xlsm\"}\n",
    "print(\"Ready. Download directory:\", WORKDIR)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Download all supported files\n",
    "\n",
    "The GitHub Contents API is used only to discover filenames; each supported file itself is fetched using `wget` from the raw-content URL."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "api_url = f\"https://api.github.com/repos/{OWNER}/{REPO}/contents/{RAW_DIR}?ref={REF}\"\n",
    "response = requests.get(api_url, timeout=30)\n",
    "response.raise_for_status()\n",
    "entries = response.json()\n",
    "if not isinstance(entries, list):\n",
    "    raise RuntimeError(f\"Expected a directory listing from GitHub, got: {entries}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "data_files = [entry for entry in entries\n",
    "              if entry.get(\"type\") == \"file\"\n",
    "              and Path(entry.get(\"name\", \"\")).suffix.lower() in SUPPORTED]\n",
    "if not data_files:\n",
    "    raise RuntimeError(\"No supported CSV/TXT/Excel files were found in the raw folder.\")\n",
    "\n",
    "for entry in data_files:\n",
    "    name = entry[\"name\"]\n",
    "    destination = WORKDIR / name\n",
    "    download_url = entry.get(\"download_url\") or (\n",
    "        f\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/{OWNER}/{REPO}/{REF}/{RAW_DIR}/{name}\")\n",
    "    print(f\"Downloading {name}\")\n",
    "    subprocess.run([\"wget\", \"--quiet\", \"--show-progress\", \"-O\",\n",
    "                    str(destination), download_url], check=True)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"\\nDownloaded {len(data_files)} supported files.\")\n",
    "[p.name for p in sorted(WORKDIR.iterdir())]"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Parse tables without converting text numbers to floats\n",
    "\n",
    "CSV/TXT numeric tokens are validated with `Decimal`, then retained as their original strings. This avoids binary-float rounding and keeps values such as `2.57864e-42` intact in the JSON output. Header lines become section labels; blank lines separate tables."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "NUMBER_RE = re.compile(r\"^[+-]?(?:(?:\\d+(?:\\.\\d*)?)|(?:\\.\\d+))(?:[eEdD][+-]?\\d+)?$\")\n",
    "\n",
    "def number_text(value):\n",
    "    \"\"\"Return a numeric token as text, or None if this cell is not numeric.\"\"\"\n",
    "    if value is None or isinstance(value, bool):\n",
    "        return None\n",
    "    # For files, leave the original decimal/scientific-notation token untouched.\n",
    "    text = str(value).strip()\n",
    "    if not text or not NUMBER_RE.fullmatch(text):\n",
    "        return None\n",
    "    try:\n",
    "        Decimal(text.replace(\"D\", \"E\").replace(\"d\", \"e\"))\n",
    "    except InvalidOperation:\n",
    "        return None\n",
    "    return text\n",
    "\n",
    "def row_to_cells(line, suffix):\n",
    "    # CSV uses proper quote-aware parsing; TXT accepts either whitespace or commas.\n",
    "    if suffix.lower() == \".csv\":\n",
    "        return next(csv.reader([line], skipinitialspace=True))\n",
    "    if \",\" in line:\n",
    "        return next(csv.reader([line], skipinitialspace=True))\n",
    "    return line.split()\n",
    "\n",
    "def parse_rows(rows):\n",
    "    \"\"\"Turn rows into separate labeled sections of two-value pairs.\"\"\"\n",
    "    sections = []\n",
    "    current_pairs = []\n",
    "    current_label = None\n",
",
    "    def flush():\n",
    "        nonlocal current_pairs, current_label\n",
    "        if current_pairs:\n",
    "            sections.append({\"label\": current_label or f\"section_{len(sections) + 1}\",\n",
    "                             \"pairs\": current_pairs})\n",
    "        current_pairs = []\n",
    "\n",
    "    for raw_row in rows:\n",
    "        cells = [\"\" if cell is None else str(cell).strip() for cell in raw_row]\n",
    "        if not any(cells):\n",
    "            flush()\n",
    "            current_label = None\n",
    "            continue\n",
    "        numeric = [number_text(cell) for cell in cells]\n",
    "        numeric = [value for value in numeric if value is not None]\n",
    "        if len(numeric) >= 2:\n",
    "            # Selecting the last two numeric fields accommodates an initial row/index column.\n",
    "            current_pairs.append(numeric[-2:])\n",
    "        else:\n",
    "            # A nonnumeric row is treated as a header/annotation, not a data point.\n",
    "            flush()\n",
    "            label_cells = [cell for cell in cells if cell]\n",
    "            if label_cells:\n",
    "                current_label = \",\".join(label_cells)\n",
    "    flush()\n",
    "    return sections\n",
    "\n",
    "def parse_text_file(path):\n",
    "    rows = []\n",
    "    with path.open(\"r\", encoding=\"utf-8-sig\", errors=\"replace\") as stream:\n",
    "        for line in stream:\n",
    "            stripped = line.strip()\n",
    "            if not stripped or stripped.startswith(\"#\") or stripped.startswith(\"#:\"):\n",
    "                # Metadata/comments are not numeric table rows.\n",
    "                continue\n",
    "            rows.append(row_to_cells(stripped, path.suffix))\n",
    "    return parse_rows(rows)\n",
    "\n",
    "def excel_cell_text(value):\n",
    "    # Excel numeric cells have no original source token. Decimal(str(value)) avoids\n",
    "    # introducing additional float arithmetic while emitting a JSON-compatible string.\n",
    "    if isinstance(value, (int, float, Decimal)) and not isinstance(value, bool):\n",
    "        return str(value)\n",
    "    return \"\" if value is None else str(value).strip()\n",
    "\n",
    "def parse_excel_file(path):\n",
    "    workbook = openpyxl.load_workbook(path, read_only=True, data_only=True)\n",
    "    sections = []\n",
    "    try:\n",
    "        for sheet in workbook.worksheets:\n",
    "            sheet_sections = parse_rows(\n",
    "                [[excel_cell_text(value) for value in row]\n",
    "                 for row in sheet.iter_rows(values_only=True)])\n",
    "            for section in sheet_sections:\n",
    "                section[\"label\"] = f\"{sheet.title}: {section['label']}\"\n",
    "            sections.extend(sheet_sections)\n",
    "    finally:\n",
    "        workbook.close()\n",
    "    return sections\n",
    "\n",
    "def parse_file(path):\n",
    "    suffix = path.suffix.lower()\n",
    "    if suffix in {\".xlsx\", \".xlsm\"}:\n",
    "        return parse_excel_file(path)\n",
    "    if suffix in {\".csv\", \".txt\"}:\n",
    "        return parse_text_file(path)\n",
    "    raise ValueError(f\"Unsupported file type: {path.name}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Convert every downloaded file and save JSON\n",
    "\n",
    "The top-level object is keyed by filename. Each value is a list of sections; each section's `pairs` field is the requested list-of-pairs shape. Unparseable files are reported rather than silently ignored."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "results = {}\n",
    "errors = {}\n",
    "for path in sorted(WORKDIR.iterdir()):\n",
    "    if path.suffix.lower() not in SUPPORTED:\n",
    "        continue\n",
    "    try:\n",
    "        sections = parse_file(path)\n",
    "        if not sections:\n",
    "            errors[path.name] = \"No numeric two-column table detected\"\n",
    "            continue\n",
    "        results[path.name] = sections\n",
    "        print(f\"{path.name}: {sum(len(s['pairs']) for s in sections)} points in {len(sections)} section(s)\")\n",
    "    except Exception as exc:\n",
    "        errors[path.name] = f\"{type(exc).__name__}: {exc}\"\n",
    "\n",
    "output_path = Path(\"/content/raw_data.json\")\n",
    "with output_path.open(\"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as stream:\n",
    "    json.dump(results, stream, ensure_ascii=False, indent=2)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"\\nWrote {output_path} ({output_path.stat().st_size:,} bytes)\")\n",
    "if errors:\n",
    "    print(\"\\nFiles needing attention:\")\n",
    "    print(json.dumps(errors, indent=2))\n",
    "\n",
    "# Example: fetch the first curve's list of pairs. Values are strings to preserve notation.\n",
    "first_file = next(iter(results))\n",
    "print(\"\\nExample file:\", first_file)\n",
    "print(\"Section:\", results[first_file][0][\"label\"])\n",
    "print(\"First pairs:\", results[first_file][0][\"pairs\"][:3])"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Download the JSON result\n",
    "\n",
    "This cell triggers a browser download in Google Colab."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "from google.colab import files\n",
    "files.download(str(output_path))"
   ]
  }
